<section class="hero theme-dark">
  {% include "partials/wind-mark.njk" %}
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1 class="hero__name">MIKAEL VIIMA</h1>
    <p class="hero__tagline">Poetry.<br>Fiction.<br>The human animal without an alibi.</p>
    <p class="hero__intro">
      Finnish writer Mikael Viima writes psychological poetry and noir about the human
      animal: desire, memory, science, mortality, power, art, absurdity — and the
      things behind masks.
    </p>
    <div class="hero__ctas">
      <a class="button" href="/books/">Read the work</a>
      <a class="button button--ghost" href="/about/">About Mikael</a>
    </div>
    <p class="hero__credibility">Published in Finland by WSOY and Otava.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="label content-section__label">Current / poetry</p>
    <h2 class="content-section__heading">FEED</h2>
    <p class="content-section__body"><em>A poetry manuscript.</em></p>
    <div class="content-section__body">
      <p>
        Physics beside grief. Sex beside death. War beside jokes. Art beside contempt
        for art. Some poems stretch across the page; some barely survive a sentence.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>FEED</strong> is built less like a themed collection than a mind under
        pressure: empirical reality, private damage, public absurdity, beauty, age,
        damage and the occasional refusal to behave.
      </p>
      <p>
        The manuscript currently contains approximately {{ current_work.poem_count_approx }}
        selected poems from a body thrice that and is being prepared by editors for
        English-language submission.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p><a class="button" href="/poetry/">Enter FEED</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="label content-section__label">Fiction / Aarni Susi</p>
    <h2 class="content-section__heading">A detective whose own mind is the least reliable room in the building.</h2>
    <div class="content-section__body">
      <p>
        The Aarni Susi novels are hard-edged psychological crime stories set in
        contemporary Helsinki. Real criminal behavior from real crime cases from
        Finland across two decades, institutional failure and damaged cognition matter
        as much as plot.
      </p>
      <p>
        The series began with <strong>Verijälki</strong> in 2022 and continued with
        <strong>Rekyyli</strong> in 2023, both published by WSOY in Finland.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="book-strip">
      {%- for book in books %}
      <a class="book-card" href="/books/{{ book.slug }}/">
        <div class="cover">
          <span class="cover__placeholder">Cover — {{ book.title }}<br>(pending art)</span>
        </div>
        <p class="book-card__title">{{ book.title }}</p>
        <p class="book-card__meta">{{ book.publisher }}, {{ book.year }}{% if book.nonfiction %} · Nonfiction{% endif %}</p>
      </a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    <p><a class="button" href="/books/">Explore the books</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="content-section__heading">Already published. Not yet finished.</h2>
    <div class="content-section__body">
      <p>
        Mikael Viima's fiction has been published in Finland by WSOY. Under his real
        name, Manne Laukkanen, he is also the author of the nonfiction book
        <strong>Vaaralliset gurut</strong>, published by Otava in 2024, as well as his
        PhD thesis, blueprinting a statistical home-prediction system to predict the
        home base of serial offenders based on their spatial and crime-site behavior.
      </p>
      <p>The next phase is outward: English-language poetry, fiction and international readership.</p>
    </div>
    <p><a class="button button--ghost" href="/books/">Books &amp; publication history</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section theme-dark pull-quote--section motif-host">
  {% include "partials/wind-mark.njk" %}
  <div class="wrap">
    <blockquote class="pull-quote">
      I am interested in the moment when the respectable explanation stops working
      and the animal underneath is forced to speak for itself.
    </blockquote>
    <p class="content-section__body">
      In a murder investigation. In a marriage. In politics. In a laboratory. In a poem.
    </p>
    <p class="content-section__body">The genres change. The narrator does not.</p>
  </div>
</section>

